"""What every part of Cuckoo Village is: the content of the parts catalogue (scripts/cuckoo-village-catalogue.py).

Pure data, read both inside Blender (catalogue_render.py, which renders each entry) and on the host (the HTML and PDF).
One entry per part. An entry is one of:

  actor    the whole actor, or `iso` (names) when many actors share one mesh and the card shows one of them
  section  one labelled piece of a bigger mesh (the `cat_sections` the part builders record: tower_art.py, bavaria.py)
  engine   an object with no picture (camera, lights, the director, the settings holder)

tests/test_cuckoo_village_catalogue.py checks that every actor in the built level (inventory.json beside the catalogue) has an
entry, so a new part cannot be added without saying what it is.

Fields: id, group, title, kind, actors (every actor the card is about; the context picture highlights all of them), iso (the one
shown on its own), section, what (a sentence or two), details (bullets), shown (what makes it visible), moves (what poses it),
ctx ('village' or 'tower': the context picture), wire (True: a wireframe view as well), mode ('classic' or 'bavaria': which set of
parts the context picture shows).
"""
